{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"3d65be730445ce3527df2d1350251c1f27dd708136ef304fb1a7e7cd3f8a81a3","digest":{"component_or_area":"README quickstart documentation","key_entities":["README.md","lines 33-53","reel-lot-tea","CLI create command","rebar create","rebar ready","rebar claim","rebar close","mcpServers config"],"problem_keywords":["quickstart","documentation","end-to-end","runnable","hard-coded id","misleading","disconnected workflow"],"propositions":["The README quickstart claims to run one ticket end-to-end across all three surfaces but does not: CLI creates a ticket then acts on unrelated hard-coded id reel-lot-tea instead of the just-created ticket.","The Python quickstart block creates a separate ticket rather than threading the same ticket through the workflow as the claim implies.","The MCP quickstart block shows only mcpServers config and performs no actual operation, despite prose implying an operation occurs.","The golden-path CI gate (ticket 0435) extracts and executes the README CLI block verbatim, requiring a single coherent runnable command sequence with no disconnected hard-coded ids.","The CLI quickstart block must capture the created ticket id and thread that same id through create → ready → claim → close as a copy-pasteable, runnable sequence with no hard-coded id."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785823574481305406,"uuid":"76edae70-30eb-499f-a3ca-a750b7e9a289"}